Affected component: OSPF default route origination on r1 (FRR daemon). Mechanism: Access switches and distribution/core switches have full OSPF adjacency and exchange internal routes, so inter-office traffic works. However, when hosts try to reach the Internet (e.g., 203.0.113.1), their first-hop DSW replies “Destination Net Unreachable” because it has no route to external networks and no OSPF-learned default. This is evidenced by PC pings failing with ICMP Net Unreachable sourced from 10.1.0.2 (dswa1 SVI) and by the absence of 0.0.0.0/0 in dswa1/csw1/csw2 routing tables. Localization: r1 FRR OSPF config has “default-information originate” but r1’s RIB has no default route, so OSPF doesn’t inject a default into the fabri
